{
  "name": "belt_by_hand",
  "description": "The whole transport ladder built the way a player builds it. Every command here is one PlayController emits from a click or a drag — {system: build} throughout, no logistics op except the two `insert` calls that stand in for a mine dropping ore into a crate. It contains, in order: an arm lifting coal out of a crate onto a dragged line; a nine-tile straight run; a sunken belt whose two mouths are four tiles apart with somebody else's line running between them; a sorting table splitting the flow into two crates; and, off to the east, a second drag that turns a corner and delivers round it. Read off state.json: logistics.totals.belts is the number of transport lines the drags produced (a corner and a tunnel each cut one), logistics.metrics.corners_turned is 1 because exactly one drag changed direction, and the crates at (38,22), (38,23), (48,23) and (29,26) hold what came down each branch. Coordinates are for seed 7 and were read off a buildability map, not guessed.",
